DECOUPLING THRESHOLD: smallest n where X is NOT a function of Y (orbit-refinement onset)
==========================================================================
X | Y              n=3   n=4   n=5   n=6   threshold
H | score          det   det SPLIT SPLIT   5
H | c3             det   det SPLIT SPLIT   5
tr4 | c3           det   det SPLIT SPLIT   5
tr4 | score        det   det SPLIT SPLIT   5
charS | score      det   det SPLIT SPLIT   5
H | charS        SPLIT SPLIT SPLIT SPLIT   3
H | tr4          SPLIT SPLIT SPLIT SPLIT   3
scc | score        det   det   det   det   >6
c3 | score         det   det   det   det   >6

 READING: threshold = the n at which the Y-orbit first refines into multiple X-values.
 If spectral/path-from-combinatorial pairs cluster at n=5 => the 'quaternion wall' conjecture.
